course: dictionary
lesson: 1823
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word coach is a good example. You can tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it. «Theo skipped football for a cold; the coach saw him at the cinema.» Here a coach is the person who trains a football team.
explain: The same word can mean a big bus too. A coach is a big comfortable bus for long trips, with seats, luggage space underneath and seat belts. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about training or travelling? That question usually tells you which meaning to pick.
explain: To coach is a verb: it means to train or teach someone a skill. «Children can share their wins with other grown-ups, like a teacher, a grandparent or a coach.» Here the coach is the grown-up who helps you get better at something.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A coach can be a person who trains a sports team or a player.
fact: A coach is also a big comfortable bus for long trips (UK).
fact: To coach means to train or teach someone a skill.
fact: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the clues in the sentence before you choose.
exercise: In «Our football coach planned the training for Saturday.» what does coach mean? | A carriage of a train | A carriage pulled by horses | *A person who trains a sports team | A bus with seats for passengers
exercise: «Our class travelled to the seaside by coach.» What is a coach in this sentence? | A horse | A person who trains a team | A carriage at the back of a train | *A big bus for long trips
exercise: What does it mean to coach someone? | To carry their bags | *To train or teach them a skill | To cheer loudly from the stands | To drive them to a match
test: In «Theo skipped football for a cold; the coach saw him at the cinema.» who saw Theo? | Theo's sister | Theo's teacher | *The coach | Theo's grandad
test: Which sentence uses coach to mean a bus? | The coach picked the best players for the final. | She wants to coach the younger players next year. | The coach encouraged the team before the match. | *The coach stopped at the services so everyone could have a break.
exam: What does coach mean in «Children can share their wins with other grown-ups, like a teacher, a grandparent or a coach.»? | A horse-drawn carriage | *A person who trains a sports team or a player | A carriage of a train | A big bus
